In my recent game, playing too fast, I got confused by an umber hulk
and killed my pet unicorn by accident. Even if I was confused I felt
guilty of course (luck-5) and I heared "the rumble of distant thunder"
(align-15). So I zapped a turn undead in hope to get back my unicorn
and to make amends for the accident that way. Though the unicorn came
back hostile - and I accepted it as the price for my rushing game; it
attacked me. But then...
I killed the hostile unicorn and, once again, got the "You feel guilty"
(and thus the luck-5 penalty).
Don't count on a fair lawsuit in Nethack; you'll be pronounced guilty
twice for the same case. :-}

Technically this seems to be always the case if you kill a unicorn of
your alignment. But then I wonder why a coaligend unicorn wouldn't be
always revived peaceful (or tame). The logic is somewhat difficult to
comprehend.

